US airports at or above the commercial enplanement floor, ordered by calculated tight-capacity passenger share in CY2025 ({F370.period}). Definition: {F370.definition}. This is a metric rank, not an investment screen, so screening flags do not apply.

1. STC — {F370}
2. PVU — {F314}
3. RFD — {F322}
4. EAT — {F119}
5. LNK — {F228}
6. SJU — {F358}
7. ERI — {F127}
8. BQN — {F59}
9. LCK — {F220}
10. AZA — {F32}

AZA {F422} outranks SGF {F423} on this same rank, and the shares {F32} and {F350} are not equal, so the cutoff is not a tie.

Average taxi-out and busiest scheduled hour cannot be established for full CY2025. On-Time coverage starts after the beginning of that year. The measures below use {F796.period} only.

The flight-weighted average taxi-out for the ranked airports that have On-Time taxi-out observations, excluding EAT, is {F796} ({F796.class}) over {F796.period}. It is total taxi-out minutes divided by flights with taxi-out, not an equal-weight mean of the airport figures. On-Time coverage for that group total is below the coverage threshold.

EAT has no On-Time rows in {F796.period}, so average taxi-out and busiest scheduled hour are not established for EAT.

Busiest scheduled hour is non-additive across airports, so there is no set total. Airport-level values are below. Taxi-out is {F778.class}. Busiest hour is {F787.class}.

1. STC — taxi-out {F786}; busiest hour {F795}
2. PVU — taxi-out {F783}; busiest hour {F792}
3. RFD — taxi-out {F784}; busiest hour {F793}
4. EAT — taxi-out and busiest hour not established
5. LNK — taxi-out {F782}; busiest hour {F791}
6. SJU — taxi-out {F785}; busiest hour {F794}
7. ERI — taxi-out {F780}; busiest hour {F789}
8. BQN — taxi-out {F779}; busiest hour {F788}
9. LCK — taxi-out {F781}; busiest hour {F790}
10. AZA — taxi-out {F778}; busiest hour {F787}

ERI {F780}, PVU {F783}, and SJU {F785} are flagged for low On-Time coverage, so taxi-out at those airports describes a partial slice. The same flag is on busiest hour for ERI {F789}, PVU {F792}, and SJU {F794}.
